<Project Sdk="Microsoft.NET.Sdk">
	<Import Project="..\Version.props" />
	<PropertyGroup>
		<AssemblyName>PeachDrawing.Abstractions</AssemblyName>
		<RootNamespace>PeachDrawing.Abstractions</RootNamespace>
		<PackageId>PeachDrawing.Abstractions</PackageId>
		<Description>The drawing-surface abstraction (Canvas, RenderContext, Brush, Pen, Font, Image, GraphicsPath and the paint-ready value types) PeachPDF targets to write PDF. A user of PeachDrawing.Abstractions can build their own render target the same way PeachPDF targets it to PDF, or take PeachDrawing's own raster Canvas implementation.</Description>
		<PackageTags>drawing;graphics;canvas;rendering-abstraction</PackageTags>
		<PackageIcon>peach.png</PackageIcon>
		<PackageProjectUrl>https://peachpdf.net/</PackageProjectUrl>
		<RepositoryUrl>https://github.com/jhaygood86/PeachPDF.git</RepositoryUrl>
		<PackageLicenseExpression>BSD-3-Clause</PackageLicenseExpression>
		<IncludeSymbols>true</IncludeSymbols>
		<GenerateDocumentationFile>true</GenerateDocumentationFile>
		<WarningsAsErrors>$(WarningsAsErrors);CS1591</WarningsAsErrors>
		<GeneratePackageOnBuild>True</GeneratePackageOnBuild>
		<GenerateAssemblyConfigurationAttribute>false</GenerateAssemblyConfigurationAttribute>
		<GenerateAssemblyCompanyAttribute>false</GenerateAssemblyCompanyAttribute>
		<GenerateAssemblyProductAttribute>false</GenerateAssemblyProductAttribute>
		<GenerateAssemblyInformationalVersionAttribute>false</GenerateAssemblyInformationalVersionAttribute>
		<GenerateAssemblyFileVersionAttribute>false</GenerateAssemblyFileVersionAttribute>
		<GenerateAssemblyTitleVersionAttribute>false</GenerateAssemblyTitleVersionAttribute>
		<GenerateAssemblyTitleAttribute>false</GenerateAssemblyTitleAttribute>
		<GenerateAssemblyVersionAttribute>false</GenerateAssemblyVersionAttribute>
		<RunCodeAnalysis>false</RunCodeAnalysis>
		<IsTrimmable>true</IsTrimmable>
		<EnableTrimAnalyzer>true</EnableTrimAnalyzer>
		<IsAotCompatible>true</IsAotCompatible>
	</PropertyGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<ProjectReference Include="..\PeachDrawing.Text\PeachDrawing.Text.csproj" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="PeachDrawing.Abstractions.Tests" />
		<!--
			Deliberate and permanent, unlike PeachDrawing.Text's own InternalsVisibleTo (which grants nothing
			to PeachPDF): step 8's public-API pass went through every member PeachPDF reached into across the
			new assembly boundary and confirmed, one by one, that each remaining internal one is not "the
			drawing API a standalone Canvas author needs" but PeachPDF's own HTML/CSS/SVG/PDF rendering
			pipeline's private coordination surface with the Canvas/RenderContext abstraction - a different
			kind of thing, the way a UI framework's own first-party controls sometimes reach past its public
			surface into truly-internal rendering hooks no third-party control needs. Concretely:
			Canvas.FormCacheOwner/InvisibleText/PrefersRasterGroups/FlattensTransparency/
			CreateTransparencyProbe/TransformScale/CurrentTransform/SvgBackdrop/BeginRasterSurface/DrawRaster
			are read or overridden only by GraphicsAdapter/RasterGraphics (the concrete PDF/raster Canvas
			implementations) and FragmentPainter/SvgRenderer (the HTML/SVG paint code that drives any Canvas
			polymorphically, per each member's own doc remarks - e.g. SvgBackdrop's "only SvgRenderer... ever
			needs to know"); RenderContext.LayoutUnitsPerPoint is overridden by PdfSharpAdapter for its own
			font-cache keying, and RasterizationDpi/TextHinting/TextStemDarkening/MaxRasterPixels/
			RasterAntiAliasing are PdfGenerateConfig-driven knobs PdfGenerator sets each render - none of
			these describe "how do I draw a rectangle," which is what the actually-public members already
			cover in full. (RenderContext's internal CreateFont/CreateFontForCodepoint/
			CreateSystemFallbackFontForCodepoint wrapper methods are a different case entirely: confirmed by
			search that PeachPDF never calls them - only FontsHandler does, which lives in this same assembly
			now, so they stay internal for that in-assembly collaboration and contribute nothing to why this
			grant exists.) BeginRasterSurface/DrawRaster stay object?-typed even after Phase B: their real
			type (RasterSurface) now lives in PeachDrawing, which this assembly cannot reference (the
			dependency runs the other way), so object? is this member's permanent shape, not a placeholder
			pending the raster backend's own extraction - both members would stay internal either way.

			PeachPDF.Tests needs the identical grant, for the reason PeachDrawing.Text.Tests does NOT need
			one from PeachDrawing.Text: PeachPDF.Tests exercises PeachPDF's own internals directly (including
			the PdfSharpAdapter/RasterGraphics members this comment already covers, e.g. setting
			RasterAntiAliasing/TextHinting directly on a test PdfSharpAdapter instance), not just PeachPDF's
			public API - unlike PeachDrawing.Abstractions.Tests below, which is this project's own internals
			test project and needs a grant on that basis regardless of what PeachPDF needs.

			PublicApi/InternalsGrantTests.cs pins the exact granted set (PeachPDF, PeachPDF.Tests,
			PeachDrawing.Abstractions.Tests, no more) the same way PeachDrawing.Text.Tests pins its own
			all-or-nothing bar - a change to this ItemGroup should be a deliberate, reviewed edit to that
			test, not a silent widening.
		-->
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="PeachPDF" />
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="PeachPDF.Tests" />
		<!--
			Added at Phase B step 3 (the raster backend's actual extraction): PeachDrawing.RasterCanvas
			overrides the same Canvas coordination members GraphicsAdapter does (CurrentTransform/
			PrefersRasterGroups/BeginRasterSurface/DrawRaster/CreateSvgGlyphPainter, etc.) - it is the second
			real Canvas implementation this internal surface was always meant for, not a new kind of consumer.
		-->
		<InternalsVisibleTo Include="PeachDrawing" />
	</ItemGroup>
	<ItemGroup>
		<None Include="..\..\LICENSE" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
		<None Include="..\..\docs\assets\img\peach.png" Pack="true" PackagePath="\" />
	</ItemGroup>
</Project>
